cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Void, or numbers it produced, in work you publish, please
  cite it as below. Please also cite the methods behind the numbers you
  report: Help > About the Void lists them.
title: "the Void"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Benyamin M.
    family-names: Garmejani
    affiliation: "Victoria University of Wellington"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
abstract: >-
  Desktop software for crystal structures and porous materials: 3D
  viewing and measurement, pore size, accessible surface area, guest
  accessibility, open metal sites, topology, powder XRD, RASPA2 input
  sets, comparison with CoRE MOF 2024, and property models.
keywords:
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - porous materials
  - crystallography
  - pore analysis
  - topology
repository-code: "https://github.com/benjen-mg/the-void"
# Zenodo's DOI for all versions (resolves to the latest).
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23578711"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23578711"
    description: "All versions of the Void (Zenodo)"
